#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""deploy/install-release: build HEE-v3's two binaries from one clean, committed tree on main and install them as one
release at RC02's path, `$HOME/.local/lib/herdr-engineering-engine-v3/releases/<manifest-sha256>/`, with `current`
naming it (HT1, `hee3-evidence/T28/HO01-T3-20260928/FLOW-CONTRACT.md` §2).

    install-release --commit <sha> --bundle <offline-bundle-dir> --deadline <seconds> [--repo R] [--prefix P]
    install-release --control             each rule refuses its plant by its own diagnostic
    install-release --count-seams FILE... the test-seam census of each file (the positive control's reader)

The policy (the manifest, its obligations, the seam census, the quiescence and target-directory decisions, the
install's digest check) is pure and reached by argument; `main` only acquires (F95). The build is a toolbox act:
the sqlite build uses the toolbox's gcc (tools/sqlite-static.py). The host reads the installed bytes back through
`flatpak-spawn --host`. The deadline is the caller's: this tool sets no time limit of its own.
"""
